[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have a goal that looks like the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">25</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The left hand side is a fully ground term, no axioms, no open terms. I would like to reduce it to a normal form and then solve this goal by <code>rfl</code>. How can I achieve this?</p>\n<p>As a note, <code>foo</code> has a lot of dependencies and changes frequently.</p>",
        "id": 614888634,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1785983192
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you have another goal which is the type of <code>?m.25</code>? If so, you might want to solve that one first (and then consider a redesign where that goal, which is presumably not a Prop so shouldn't be being dealt with in tactic mode  never appears).</p>",
        "id": 614906379,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1785994304
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But does <code>rfl</code> not work already?</p>",
        "id": 614906457,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1785994347
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Tactic-Proofs/Tactic-Reference/#cbv\">cbv</a> does what you want?</p>",
        "id": 614912987,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1785997961
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"574718\">@Michael Sammler</span>, The type of the goals <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"955633\">@Gregory Malecha</span> is talking about might depend on external functions (like hashing in <code>Std.HashMap</code>). More specifically, it could look like a following goal:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"2\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">get?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- rfl/cbv/native_decide fail</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Both <code>rfl</code> and <code>cbv</code> fail because <code>HashMap</code> look up uses external C++ code, and <code>native_decide</code> because of the metavariable. <br>\n<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"644702\">@Wojciech Różowski</span>, I remember you have been working on <code>cbv</code>, could you please tell us if there are any ways to make it work with hash maps?</p>",
        "id": 614930083,
        "sender_full_name": "Vladimir Gladstein",
        "timestamp": 1786004058
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Seems like a specific problem with/missing annotations for <code>ofList</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emptyWithCapacity</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"2\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">get?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cbv</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>HashMap</code> look up uses external C++ code</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><del>No</del>Yes but we can still prove all interesting theorems :)</p>",
        "id": 614931294,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1786004476
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just to add more context to what <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110024\">@Sebastian Ullrich</span>  has just said.</p>\n<p><code>HashMap</code> implementation contains a reference to an opaque <code>System.Platform.numBits</code>, but its external interface contains several lemmas that allow to prove things about them. These proofs rely on a model defined in terms of associative lists.</p>\n<p><code>cbv</code> can use such external interfaces, when appropriately annotated with <code>cbv_opaque</code> and <code>cbv_eval</code> annotations.</p>",
        "id": 614971450,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1786018397
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, the following will work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">cbv_eval</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofList_eq_insertMany_empty</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">cbv_eval</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insertMany_nil</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">cbv_eval</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insertMany_cons</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"2\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">get?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cbv</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 614996792,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1786025455
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I will make a PR that adds these annotations, so it works out of the box</p>",
        "id": 614996889,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1786025480
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Out of curiosity, is it the case that functions with <code>cbv_eval</code> should usually also be <code>cbv_opaque</code> so that they don't accidentally reduce in other cases? Perhaps related, it also seems like the timeout of the initial example was specific to using string keys</p>",
        "id": 615014327,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1786029877
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, exactly! If we don't want to unroll, then we should use <code>cbv_opaque</code>, however, we can in principle use <code>cbv_eval</code> to just register non-standard equations that are tried before the registered equations, but fallback to them if they don't work</p>",
        "id": 615032323,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1786035355
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"644702\">@Wojciech Różowski</span> and <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110024\">@Sebastian Ullrich</span> <br>\nCould you please tell me what would be an asymptotics of <code>cbv</code> \"execution\" of <code>get?</code> in this case. <br>\nI am wondering, if I never actually execute my HashMap, but only use it in proofs, will it help to reduce generated proof sizes for big maps? <br>\nOr is it better to use just associate lists.</p>",
        "id": 615221814,
        "sender_full_name": "Vladimir Gladstein",
        "timestamp": 1786114067
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cbv effectively simulates an assoclist for a hashmap</p>",
        "id": 615222715,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1786114310
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>except entries will never get overridden or erased</p>",
        "id": 615222847,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786114342
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Std.TreeMap</code> will certainly have better performance</p>",
        "id": 615222946,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786114364
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Should be <code>O(log n)</code> (for <code>TreeMap.get?</code>) but I don't know how large the constant is</p>",
        "id": 615223133,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786114409
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah the constant is probably very large...</p>",
        "id": 615224189,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786114692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I actually did some benchmarks in this regard recently and <code>rfl</code> seems to reduce some basic <code>TreeMap</code> stuff better than <code>cbv</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">maxRecDepth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">9999999</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TreeSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">128</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">contains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">127</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">maxRecDepth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">9999999</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TreeSet</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">128</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">contains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">127</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide_cbv</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 615224489,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1786114779
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah here's also a little benchmark on how hash and tree sets compare:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fillHash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fillHash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fillTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TreeSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TreeSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fillTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">containsHash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HashSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">contains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">containsHash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">containsTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TreeSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">contains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">containsTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tk</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"count_heartbeats \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tac</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getNumHeartbeats</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tac</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getNumHeartbeats</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfoAt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Heartbeats: {hb' - hb}\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">maxRecDepth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">containsHash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fillHash</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">160</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">160</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count_heartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cbv</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">containsTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fillTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">160</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">160</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count_heartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">containsTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fillTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">160</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">160</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count_heartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cbv</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Seems like hash sets work fairly well (even though they essentially are associate lists here) but using <code>rfl</code> with tree sets is faster; however, using <code>cbv</code> with tree sets is slower than both of the alternatives.</p>",
        "id": 615226188,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786115191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, tree sets have no cbv annotations and the tactic simulates the whole reduction that rfl does, but at the level of elaboration</p>",
        "id": 615227389,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1786115510
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unlike hash sets, tree sets do not contain anything opaque in their implementation and hence didn’t need any annotations, but one of course can use them</p>",
        "id": 615227634,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1786115571
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Of course but I suspect there is potential for having tree maps perform better than hash maps in <code>cbv</code> as well</p>",
        "id": 615228084,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786115693
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure we're getting <code>O(n log n)</code> here as we should (or maybe the constants are just trash)</p>",
        "id": 615228388,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786115756
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><img alt=\"fitplot.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1200x825\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/PbF__lGDUL4aDssYNb8GJSsf/fitplot.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/PbF__lGDUL4aDssYNb8GJSsf/fitplot.png/840x560.webp\"></p>\n<p>I think the asymptotics are right</p>",
        "id": 615230608,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1786116345
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And the first one is <code>n²</code>, as you'd expect?</p>",
        "id": 615232414,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786116819
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The hash set one?</p>",
        "id": 615232443,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786116826
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><img alt=\"fitplot.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1200x825\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/edz6n1W1nlMTn_o6FVHJxKPF/fitplot.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/edz6n1W1nlMTn_o6FVHJxKPF/fitplot.png/840x560.webp\"></p>\n<p>yup</p>",
        "id": 615233337,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1786117082
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alright but yeah the constants for tree maps are way worse, <code>754 n²</code> vs <code>42724 n ln(n)</code> oof</p>",
        "id": 615239369,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786118736
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Btw, on the topic of making <code>cbv</code> faster, what about using special \"tree\" arrays? I did a basic test and it seems like for a well-written <code>TreeArray</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkRangeTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TreeArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkRangeTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkRangeArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkRangeArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">maxHeartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Heartbeats: 476020258</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkRangeTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TreeArray</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100000</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100000</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count_heartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">kernel</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Heartbeats: 540652535</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkRangeArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1200</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count_heartbeats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">kernel</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Perhaps we should also add special support for <code>Array</code>s in <code>cbv</code> using some kind of tree array to get this kind of performance for <code>Array</code>s with <code>cbv</code>?</p>",
        "id": 615249303,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1786122152
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the insights here, it seems like a deeper problem than I thought! <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"690517\">@Vladimir Gladstein</span> helped switch the goal to use <code>TreeMap</code> and things worked out.</p>",
        "id": 615351908,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1786187828
    }
]